By the later game, you get more nutrition than you'd ever want from
corpses.  =oSlowDigestion is peripherally useful, but probably less
useful than, say, an =hunger (starving to death after minetown/sokoban
is never an issue, needing to get down from satiated occasionally is).
Neither is all that useful, though neither is completely useless.

Exceptions are if you're doing some weird repetitive strategy (extreme
altar camping) or a foodless/vegan/etc conduct.  Then =oSD can be quite
handy indeed.  But for a first-time ascension guide, recommending odd
conducts is out of scope.



